.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-diff 1  "dfdu-diff " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-diff \- What grew: a directory now against its last recorded scan (or one from \-\-since ago), or two saved scans
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu diff\fR [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-mft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
What grew: a directory now against its last recorded scan (or one from \-\-since ago), or two saved scans
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<AGE>\fR
Compare with the recorded scan closest to this long ago (`7d`, `2w`, `12h`) instead of the last one
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 3]
Levels below the root to list
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR [default: 30]
Changes to list, largest first
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-change\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR [default: 1M]
Leave out changes smaller than this (`1M`, `500K`)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output: table or json (schema/diff.v1.json)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-mft\fR
Windows, as administrator: read each NTFS volume\*(Aqs master file table instead of listing its directories, which is much faster on large volumes. Volumes whose table cannot be read are listed as usual
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
A directory, scanned now and compared with its last recorded scan; or two files (a snapshot or an ncdu export each), the older first
